  "problem": "$5{\\text{i}}^{-2}=$",
  "worked_solution": "First, using the laws of exponents, we can write\n\n$$\n5{\\text{i}}^{-2}=\\frac{5}{{\\text{i}}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe now recall that ${\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{{\\text{i}}^{2}}=\\frac{5}{(-1)}=-5.\n$$",
